PROVED (+checked j<2^13): row r at height h = {odd u : u = b_r 2^{-h} mod 9}, an arithmetic progression of step 18
   at index positions j = j0 mod 2^{h+1}; the row is the 2-adic interleaving of these six-periodic AP layers.
   This is exactly the user's 'chain segments grow a pair at a time and are interleaved'.

   row 1: indices of a fixed core satisfy j_{t+1} = 64 j_t + 14  (7(1+3r)/2), heights h0+6t.
   row 3: indices of a fixed core satisfy j_{t+1} = 64 j_t + 35  (7(1+3r)/2), heights h0+6t.
   row 5: indices of a fixed core satisfy j_{t+1} = 64 j_t + 56  (7(1+3r)/2), heights h0+6t.
PROVED: j_t = (2^{h0+6t} u - b_r)/9, so j_{t+1} - 64 j_t = 63 b_r/9 = 7 b_r = 14, 35, 56 for r=1,3,5. The 63 again.

