PROVED: the index of core u at height h in its row is (2^h u - b_r)/9, so within j<=J the core u appears at exactly
   the heights with 2^h u <= 9J + 8 in its parity class: about (1/2) log_2((9J+8)/u) times per row.  Small u is
   prominent because 2^h u is small.  1, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17 are the least cores of the six classes mod 18;
   1 and 7 are the least 1-mod-6 cores (odd heights), 5 and 11 the least 5-mod-6 cores (even heights); 7 is the
   least 1-mod-6 core >1 and 5 the least 5-mod-6 core.  'Prominence' is size, not a dynamical property.

